// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row destructure_param_move_elem_double_free (tier 1). A
// DESTRUCTURE PARAMETER whose bound element is a MOVE type double-frees at run
// time: `fn probe((s, b): (String, i64))` compiles clean, prints nothing, and
// aborts with "free(): double free detected in tcache 2" (exit 134, valgrind
// "Invalid free()" inside the callee). Rust: exit 0.
// THE PROPERTY, ENUMERATED OVER THE FIVE COPIES OF THE HAND-ROLLED
// IRREFUTABLE-DESTRUCTURE WALKER (2026-09-06h): a copy that emits `let user =
// <source>.<k>;` must mark the source place MOVED, or the source's scope-exit
// Drop runs on a payload the binding now owns. Two copies do it and are clean —
// sema_stmt.cpp emit_nested_pat_destructure ("without it: double drop", its own
// words) and the let-position array/struct destructure. THREE do not, and all
// three abort:
//   sema_decl.cpp:1497  fn-param TUPLE prologue   `fn f((s, b): (String, i64))`
//   sema_decl.cpp:1519  fn-param STRUCT prologue  `fn f(P { s, n }: P)`
//   sema_expr.cpp:17303 closure TUPLE prologue    `|(s, b): (String, i64)|`
// ONE ROW for the missing `mark_moved_expr`; the three prologues are its
// members. The `for`-header copy and the `let` copy are the CONTROLS and are
// valgrind-clean on the same shape.
package destructure_param_move_elem_double_free;
fn probe((s, b): (String, i64)) -> i64 {
    return (s.len() as i64) + b;
}
fn main() -> i32 {
    let t: (String, i64) = (String::from("abcde"), 2i64);
    if probe(t) != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
